WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.488
All the residents of Greenwood Forest were excited. Spring was finally here.

2
00:00:06.489 --> 00:00:10.912
The weather was warm, and the flowers were blooming.

3
00:00:10.913 --> 00:00:16.904
"Chirp, chirp, chirp! Spring is here! Spring is here!

4
00:00:16.905 --> 00:00:20.669
Chirp, chirp, chirp!" sang out Rosie.

5
00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:24.231
"Hey, it’s my turn to announce spring!

6
00:00:24.232 --> 00:00:29.899
You did it last year!" cried Maggie, Rosie’s twin sister.

7
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.721
Old friends were sharing stories about the winter.

8
00:00:33.722 --> 00:00:39.980
"It was the most awful winter of my life!" cried Sandy the squirrel.

9
00:00:39.981 --> 00:00:45.798
"Some days I couldn’t find a single nut to give to my children."

10
00:00:45.799 --> 00:00:49.741
New friends were also moving into the forest.

11
00:00:49.742 --> 00:00:52.952
"Hello, everyone. I’m Rhoda.

12
00:00:52.953 --> 00:00:58.062
These are my children, Kit and Katie," said Rhoda the rabbit.

13
00:00:58.063 --> 00:01:02.543
All the animals and birds in Greenwood welcomed Rhoda’s family.

14
00:01:02.544 --> 00:01:08.948
"You’re just in time to see Bella," said Henrietta the old owl.

15
00:01:08.949 --> 00:01:12.812
"Who’s Bella?" asked Katie.

16
00:01:12.813 --> 00:01:21.848
"Bella is a bear, and she is coming out of her hibernation," answered Pinkey the snake.

17
00:01:21.849 --> 00:01:26.644
"Hibernation? What does that mean?" asked Kit.

18
00:01:26.645 --> 00:01:32.514
"Come along. You can ask Bella yourself," said Henrietta.

19
00:01:32.515 --> 00:01:34.892
"Yes, let us hurry.

20
00:01:34.893 --> 00:01:40.559
We want to welcome Bella when she comes out of her cave," said Sandy.

21
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:48.033
The residents of Greenwood skipped, hopped, crawled, flew, and jumped to the entrance of a dark cave.

22
00:01:48.034 --> 00:01:57.880
Everyone stood and waited quietly. Suddenly there was a loud roar!

23
00:01:57.881 --> 00:02:02.093
"Mommy, I’m scared," cried Katie.

24
00:02:02.094 --> 00:02:06.661
"Don’t worry, dear. That’s just Bella yawning.

25
00:02:06.662 --> 00:02:12.853
She’s been sleeping for a long time." Henrietta chuckled.

26
00:02:12.854 --> 00:02:17.982
The ground began to shake. Thump! Thump! Thump!

27
00:02:17.983 --> 00:02:23.130
A big brown bear with sleepy eyes poked her head out of the cave.

28
00:02:23.131 --> 00:02:28.131
"Bella!" cheered her friends.

29
00:02:28.132 --> 00:02:35.569
"Oh, is it springtime already?" Bella asked sleepily.

30
00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:41.852
"Yes! It’s springtime! It’s springtime!" chirped Maggie.

31
00:02:41.853 --> 00:02:45.382
Bella stood on her feet and stretched her body.

32
00:02:45.383 --> 00:02:50.421
She was very tall and very big!

33
00:02:50.422 --> 00:02:57.785
"Who are they? Hello. I don’t think I know you," Bella said to Rhoda.

34
00:02:57.786 --> 00:03:03.983
"I’m Rhoda Rabbit. We just moved into Greenwood Forest," said Rhoda.

35
00:03:03.984 --> 00:03:07.873
"These are Kit and Katie, my children."

36
00:03:07.874 --> 00:03:09.877
"Don’t be frightened!

37
00:03:09.878 --> 00:03:17.100
I promise I won’t eat you, even though I am very hungry," Bella said with a smile.

38
00:03:17.101 --> 00:03:26.799
Katie poked her head out and said timidly, "What does hibernation mean?"

39
00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:31.678
"Winter is very cold, and it is hard to find food.

40
00:03:31.679 --> 00:03:37.290
So bears, like me, eat a lot of food right before winter comes.

41
00:03:37.291 --> 00:03:45.711
Then, when winter arrives, we go into our caves or trees and rest," answered Bella.

42
00:03:45.712 --> 00:03:50.969
"Do you sleep the whole time?" asked Kit, hiding behind her mother.

43
00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:57.101
"We sleep a lot, but not the whole time. We don’t like to move very much.

44
00:03:57.102 --> 00:04:03.476
Otherwise our bodies might want to wake up, and we would get hungry again.

45
00:04:03.477 --> 00:04:13.118
As long as we stay still, our heart beat becomes very slow, and our body temperature drops lower than normal," answered Bella.

46
00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:18.589
"It keeps us from getting hungry too soon."

47
00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:22.974
"How long do you hibernate?" asked Katie.

48
00:04:22.975 --> 00:04:30.301
"Usually from the beginning of October until springtime," answered Bella, smiling.

49
00:04:30.302 --> 00:04:37.091
"Are you the only one who hibernates?" asked Kit, still hiding.

50
00:04:37.092 --> 00:04:42.336
"Frogs, bats, and snakes hibernate as well," answered Bella.

51
00:04:42.337 --> 00:04:45.097
Kit and Katie were amazed.

52
00:04:45.098 --> 00:04:49.036
They had never met someone who had slept for so long!

53
00:04:49.037 --> 00:04:54.288
"Thank you all for welcoming me into spring," said Bella.

54
00:04:54.289 --> 00:04:58.837
"It’s good to see you, Bella!" cried her friends.

55
00:04:58.838 --> 00:05:03.686
"Well, the welcome party is over," said Henrietta.

56
00:05:03.687 --> 00:05:09.139
"Spring is here, and we have a lot of work to do."

57
00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:12.316
"Work?" asked Katie.

58
00:05:12.317 --> 00:05:22.663
"Of course. Now that the sunshine is here and the weather is warmer, we must prepare for next winter, before it gets cold again," said Sandy.

59
00:05:22.665 --> 00:05:29.173
"Don’t worry," chuckled Bella, seeing the gloomy expressions on the rabbits’ faces.

60
00:05:29.174 --> 00:05:33.515
"We will have lots of fun too."

61
00:05:33.516 --> 00:05:38.687
The animals returned to the center of the forest, looking for food along the way.

62
00:05:38.688 --> 00:05:46.551
As they left, they shouted to Rhoda, Kit, and Katie, "Welcome to Greenwood Forest!"

63
00:05:46.552 --> 00:05:51.290
"Thank you!" the rabbits replied.

64
00:05:51.291 --> 00:05:55.717
"I guess we had better go too," said Rhoda.

65
00:05:55.718 --> 00:06:01.109
And they hopped off to find a burrow in their new forest.

66
00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:05.597
"Spring is here! Spring is here!" chirped Maggie.

67
00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:11.331
"No, it’s my turn! It’s springtime! It's springtime!"

68
00:06:11.332 --> 00:06:15.960
Rosie shouted happily. The two birds flew off into the sunshine.

